# A list mapped element by element from a source list that list.UniqueItems constrains into a target list that list.MaxItems bounds: the source validator may bound the length, which the checker does not read (#163).
-- source.cue --
import "list"
items: [...int] & list.UniqueItems()
-- target.cue --
import "list"
items: [...int] & list.MaxItems(2)
-- lens.cue --
v0_0: _
v1_0: {items: [for x in v0_0.items {x}]}
-- out --
unknown
v1_0.items has one element per element of v0_0.items, whose length is within [0, +inf], where the target list's length must be [0, 2]; list.UniqueItems may narrow the source's lengths further, which the checker does not read (rule unknown-copy) @ lens.cue:2:8
